# Testing Conventions

## Backend (Jest)
- Tests live under [backend/src/tests](mdc:backend/src/tests) and mirror layer intent:
  - Domain: [backend/src/tests/domain](mdc:backend/src/tests/domain)
  - Integration: [backend/src/tests/integration](mdc:backend/src/tests/integration)
  - E2E: [backend/src/tests/e2e](mdc:backend/src/tests/e2e)
- Use test DB setup from [backend/src/tests/database](mdc:backend/src/tests/database) for integration/e2e.
- Prefer testing use-cases via public interfaces; mock repositories when unit testing.

## Frontend (Jest + RTL)
- Component tests under [frontend/src/tests/components](mdc:frontend/src/tests/components)
- App-level tests in [frontend/src/tests/App.test.tsx](mdc:frontend/src/tests/App.test.tsx)
- Use React Testing Library queries; avoid implementation details.

## Naming & Practices
- Name files `*.test.ts` or `*.test.tsx` alongside or in `tests/`.
- Keep tests deterministic; avoid real network and rely on mocks except in e2e.
- Arrange-Act-Assert structure; prefer high-signal assertions.

